{
  "_note": "Seven schemes in the solid_body character: one continuous mass, no court, no hole through the plan. Because a solid body forfeits plan void, every scheme takes its articulation from SECTION - the plan is made to change as the body rises (terracing, stagger, shear, axis swap, prow, twist, counterpoise). Fractions of the buildable plan and the legal height. Stacked volumes overlap ~0.02 in z and share generous plan overlap so the result is one boolean body, never a shared exact face and never a gap. Volume heights are held within 2x inside each scheme and no volume carries more plan area than the one under it.",
